WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.210
JAMIE: I contain multitudes.

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:05.624
ALEX: Okay, but here's what I'm
genuinely curious about. For someone who
is

00:00:05.624 --> 00:00:08.859
ALEX: evaluating AI infrastructure right
now — say you're running a mid-size
company

00:00:08.859 --> 00:00:12.094
ALEX: with a real agentic use case
you're trying to build — does

00:00:12.094 --> 00:00:15.328
ALEX: this change your calculus?

00:00:15.413 --> 00:00:18.598
RUFUS: Possibly. If you've been holding
off on committing to a hardware vendor

00:00:18.598 --> 00:00:21.783
RUFUS: because you didn't want to be
entirely at the mercy of cloud

00:00:21.783 --> 00:00:24.969
RUFUS: pricing, this gives you another
option to evaluate. It's not Nvidia-
versus-Google yet.

00:00:24.969 --> 00:00:28.154
RUFUS: But it's the clearest signal that
Google wants to be in that

00:00:28.154 --> 00:00:31.339
RUFUS: conversation.
